[7.411012, "o", "cat target_iptables.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[7.411927, "o", "*filter\r\n:INPUT DROP [0:0]\r\n:FORWARD DROP [0:0]\r\n:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]\r\n-A INPUT -i lo -j ACCEPT\r\n-A INPUT -m state --state ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT\r\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 22 -j ACCEPT\r\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -m string --string \"Mozilla\" --algo bm -j ACCEPT\r\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -m string --string \"Mozilla\" --algo bm -j ACCEPT\r\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -j DROP\r\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -j DROP\r\n-A INPUT -p icmp --icmp-type echo-request -j ACCEPT\r\nCOMMIT\r\n"]
[7.412066, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[7.412098, "o", "user@169be8705533:~/pentest$ "]
[31.027293, "i", "cat > finding.txt << 'EOF'\nFINDING: HTTP/HTTPS Traffic Blocking Issue\n\nAFFECTED RULES:\n- Rule 7: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -m string --string \"Mozilla\" --algo bm -j ACCEPT\n- Rule 8: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -m string --string \"Mozilla\" --algo bm -j ACCEPT\n- Rule 9: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -j DROP\n- Rule 10: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -j DROP\n\nROOT CAUSE:\nThe iptables ruleset implements a flawed User-Agent filtering mechanism. Rules 7-8 only accept HTTP/HTTPS traffic if the packet contains the string \"Mozilla\" (attempting to filter by browser type). Rules 9-10 then explicitly DROP all other HTTP/HTTPS traffic that doesn't match.\n\nWHY SSH WORKS BUT HTTP DOESN'T:\n- SSH (port 22): Has an unconditional ACCEPT rule with no string matching requirements\n- HTTP/HTTPS (ports 80/443): Require packets to contain \"Mozilla\" string to be accepted\n\nWHY CURL HANGS:\nThe curl command sends a User-Agent header like \"curl/7.x.x\" which does not contain the string \"Mozilla\". Therefore:\n1. The packet doesn't match rules 7-8 "]
[31.027344, "i", "(no \"Mozilla\" string found)\n2. The packet hits rules 9-10 and gets DROPped (not REJECTed)\n3. Since DROP silently discards packets, curl waits indefinitely for a response that never comes\n\nRECOMMENDATION:\nThis string-matching approach for access control is fundamentally flawed:\n- It can be trivially bypassed by adding \"Mozilla\" to any User-Agent\n- It blocks legitimate tools (curl, wget, scripts, monitoring systems, APIs)\n- String matching on packet payload is CPU-intensive and unreliable\n- It provides no real security benefit\n\nThe organization should remove rules 7-10 and implement proper access controls using:\n- Source IP whitelisting (-s flag)\n- Network-based restrictions (firewall zones)\n- Application-layer authentication (not firewall rules)\nEOF\n"]
[31.027743, "o", "cat > finding.txt << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.027787, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.027817, "o", "> "]
[31.027922, "o", "FINDING: HTTP/HTTPS Traffic Blocking Issue\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.027969, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.027992, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.028039, "o", "AFFECTED RULES:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.028068, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.028373, "o", "- Rule 7: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -m string --string \"Mozilla\" --algo bm -j ACCEPT\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.02842, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.028648, "o", "- Rule 8: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -m string --string \"Mozilla\" --algo bm -j ACCEPT\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.028693, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.028805, "o", "- Rule 9: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -j DROP\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.028831, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.028857, "o", "> "]
[31.02898, "o", "- Rule 10: -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -j DROP\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.029012, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.029044, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.029085, "o", "ROOT CAUSE:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.029117, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.029911, "o", "The iptables ruleset implements a flawed User-Agent filtering mechanism. Rules 7-8 only accept HTTP/HTTPS traffic if the packet contains the string \"Mozilla\" (attempting to filter by browser type). Rules 9-10 then explicitly DROP all other HTTP/HTTPS traffic that doesn't match.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.029972, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.030064, "o", "WHY SSH WORKS BUT HTTP DOESN'T:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.030099, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.030357, "o", "- SSH (port 22): Has an unconditional ACCEPT rule with no string matching requirements\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.030383, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.030412, "o", "> "]
[31.030637, "o", "- HTTP/HTTPS (ports 80/443): Require packets to contain \"Mozilla\" string to be accepted\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.030667, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.030694, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.030722, "o", "> "]
[31.030752, "o", "WHY CURL HANGS:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.030781, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.031124, "o", "The curl command sends a User-Agent header like \"curl/7.x.x\" which does not contain the string \"Mozilla\". Therefore:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.031166, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.031358, "o", "1. The packet doesn't match rules 7-8 (no \"Mozilla\" string found)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.0314, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.031568, "o", "2. The packet hits rules 9-10 and gets DROPped (not REJECTed)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.031598, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.031868, "o", "3. Since DROP silently discards packets, curl waits indefinitely for a response that never comes\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.031897, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.031925, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.031977, "o", "RECOMMENDATION:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.032007, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.032219, "o", "This string-matching approach for access control is fundamentally flawed:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.032257, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.032459, "o", "- It can be trivially bypassed by adding \"Mozilla\" to any User-Agent\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.03249, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.032707, "o", "- It blocks legitimate tools (curl, wget, scripts, monitoring systems, APIs)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.032739, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.032928, "o", "- String matching on packet payload is CPU-intensive and unreliable\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.032959, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.033074, "o", "- It provides no real security benefit\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.033106, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.033137, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.033397, "o", "The organization should remove rules 7-10 and implement proper access controls using:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.033424, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.03344, "o", "> "]
[31.033533, "o", "- Source IP whitelisting (-s flag)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.033556, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[31.033583, "o", "> "]
[31.033695, "o", "- Network-based restrictions (firewall zones)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[31.033725, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[31.033889, "o", "- Application-layer authentication (not firewall rules)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
